# A relayed DHCPDISCOVER of a Windows 11 client whose MAC has a reservation keyed by MAC
# (WP8.4, the reservation identity): client identifier type 1 with the MAC, maximum
# message size 1500, host name, vendor class MSFT 5.0 and the Windows parameter request
# list; padded to 300 octets. The reservation holds although the client's identity is its
# option 61. Modelled by hand on the option order and parameter request list this client
# sends; documentation addresses (RFC 5737) and MACs (RFC 7042).
#
# op 1, htype 1, hlen 6, hops 1
01 01 06 01
# xid
a1 01 20 61
# secs, flags
00 00 00 00
# ciaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# yiaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# siaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# giaddr 192.0.2.1
c0 00 02 01
# chaddr: the reserved MAC
00 00 5e 00 53 20 00*10
# sname: empty
00*64
# file: empty
00*128
# magic cookie
63 82 53 63
# option 53: DHCPDISCOVER
35 01 01
# option 61: client identifier, type 1 and the MAC
3d 07 01 00 00 5e 00 53 20
# option 57: maximum message size 1500
39 02 05 dc
# option 12: host name "WS-20"
0c 05 57 53 2d 32 30
# option 60: vendor class identifier "MSFT 5.0"
3c 08 4d 53 46 54 20 35 2e 30
# option 55: parameter request list
37 0e 01 03 06 0f 1f 21 2b 2c 2e 2f 77 79 f9 fc
# end
ff
# padding to 300 octets
00*10
